Experiment I-A: segmentation-conditioned object identity audit. The frozen
foundation backbone never receives object labels. Linear probes are trained on
image-disjoint PSG training objects and evaluated on the held-out PSG split.
Box ROI, ground-truth mask, and optional predicted-mask features are compared
under one object ontology.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --psg_train_ann PSG_TRAIN_ANN
  --psg_eval_ann PSG_EVAL_ANN
  --image_root IMAGE_ROOT
  --panoptic_root PANOPTIC_ROOT
  --predicted_mask_train_dir PREDICTED_MASK_TRAIN_DIR
  --predicted_mask_eval_dir PREDICTED_MASK_EVAL_DIR
  --train_cache TRAIN_CACHE
  --eval_cache EVAL_CACHE
  --source_summary SOURCE_SUMMARY
                        Formal source summary supplying ontology and mask
                        provenance in cache-only mode.
  --backbone BACKBONE
  --output_dir OUTPUT_DIR
  --cache_dir CACHE_DIR
  --train_samples TRAIN_SAMPLES
  --eval_samples EVAL_SAMPLES
  --seeds SEEDS [SEEDS ...]
  --validation_fraction VALIDATION_FRACTION
  --probe_epochs PROBE_EPOCHS
  --early_stopping_patience EARLY_STOPPING_PATIENCE
  --early_stopping_min_delta EARLY_STOPPING_MIN_DELTA
  --feature_normalization {none,zscore,l2}
                        Fit normalization on probe-training objects only;
                        apply unchanged to validation/eval.
  --probe_batch_size PROBE_BATCH_SIZE
  --learning_rate LEARNING_RATE
  --weight_decay WEIGHT_DECAY
  --roi_chunk_size ROI_CHUNK_SIZE
  --device DEVICE
